en so  there's going to have to be consequences  the second big event is our favorite  fugitives plans to rob the canon  headquarters  when de bruyne demands to know what  they're up to swanny simply responds  being outlaws they get a ride in the  hearse where they have to share a coffin  just in case marshall deffy is doing  surveillance  while they're in there we get the idea  that they're actually a couple  and as swanny starts farting we see the  syrup of epicac is starting to wreck her  system  they still go ahead with the robbery  which is certainly more difficult as a  result of all the puking and farting  there is some suspense as things unfold  but most of it comes from swanny's  distress  as she's losing control over bodily  functions  in the end they make it out with twenty  thousand dollars but with three people  dead it's gonna wind up being about more  than just the money  the episode ends with lloyd taking stock  of the situation  dr senator tells him he thinks it could  be a coordinated action and that would  mean the start of an all-out war  loy's not really sure what to do next  because he can't really make sense of  why this is happening after all they  have each other's kids  doctor wonders who gave the order the  boss or the brother and puts it out  there that the fadas might be fighting  with each other  and he lays it out there he says once we  start shooting back it's to the death  so we better be sure and then the  credits roll  so now we can see how everything is  starting to come together things are  escalating and it's interesting that  orienta  influenced both of the big events of the  episode by  offing donatello she created the power  struggle  between the fada brothers her pie also  led to the robbery getting messy and  that was at least partially responsible  for the chaos that led to the gang  members getting  shot for me she still stands out as the  most intriguing character  and i thought swanny came in right  behind her on that l